# SHA-locked artifacts: the model promotion gate (verify_promotion) and the golden/baseline checks hash
# the EXACT file bytes, so these must stay byte-identical across platforms. Disable EOL conversion
# (-text); otherwise a Windows CRLF checkout changes the bytes and the SHA gate fails: the artifact
# reads as "tampered or stale" and a promoted model can never load (canary/active fail closed to no-blend).
assets/models/** -text
docs/baselines/** -text

# Universal Robots' description config, vendored byte for byte as its pinned commit holds it and
# held by scripts/arms/ur_ros2_description.sha256. A CRLF checkout would change every YAML's
# bytes and fail that pin.
scripts/arms/ur_ros2_description/** -text

# A shell script runs under bash, which refuses a CRLF line end: scripts/ursim/ursim.sh checked out on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) failed with "$'\r': command not found" until a copy was stripped by hand.
*.sh text eol=lf
